{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ECC",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I said in my heart, Come now, I will prove thee with mirth, therefore enjoy pleasure: and behold, this also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I said of laughter, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mad: and of mirth, What doeth it?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I sought in my heart, to give myself to wine, yet acquainting my heart with wisdom; and to lay hold on folly, till I might see what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that good for the sons of men, which they should do under the heaven all the days of their life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I made me great works; I built me houses; I planted me vineyards:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I made me gardens and orchards, and I planted trees in them of all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "kind of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fruits:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I made me pools of water, to water with them the wood that bringeth forth trees:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I procured ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " servants and maidens, and had servants born in my house; also I had great possessions of great and small cattle above all that were in Jerusalem before me:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I gathered me also silver and gold, and the peculiar treasure of kings, and of the provinces: I procured me men-singers and women-singers, and the delights of the sons of men, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " musical instruments, and of all sorts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So I was great, and increased more than all that were before me in Jerusalem: also my wisdom remained with me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And whatever my eyes desired I kept not from them, I withheld not my heart from any joy; for my heart rejoiced in all my labor: and this was my portion of all my labor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then I looked on all the works that my hands had wrought, and on the labor that I had labored to do: and behold, all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity and vexation of spirit, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no profit under the sun.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I turned myself to behold wisdom, and madness, and folly: for what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "can",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "do",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that cometh after the king? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that which hath been already done.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then I saw that wisdom excelleth folly, as far as light excelleth darkness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wise man's eyes ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in his head; but the fool walketh in darkness: and I myself perceived also that one event happeneth to them all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said I in my heart, As it happeneth to the fool, so it happeneth even to me; and why was I then more wise? Then I said in my heart, that this also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no remembrance of the wise more than of the fool for ever; seeing that which now ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the days to come shall all be forgotten. And how dieth the wise ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "? as the fool.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I hated life; because the work that is wrought under the sun ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " grievous to me: for all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity and vexation of spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, I hated all my labor which I had taken under the sun: because I should leave it to the man that shall be after me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And who knoweth whether he shall be a wise ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " or a fool? yet shall he have rule over all my labor in which I have labored, and in which I have showed myself wise under the sun. This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " also vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I went about to cause my heart to despair of all the labor which I took under the sun.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For there is a man whose labor is in wisdom, and in knowledge, and in equity; yet to a man that hath not labored in it, shall he leave it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his portion. This also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity and a great evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For what hath man of all his labor, and of the vexation of his heart, in which he hath labored under the sun?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For all his days ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sorrows, and his labor grief; yes, his heart taketh not rest in the night. This is also vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " nothing better for a man than that he should eat and drink, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he should make his soul enjoy good in his labor. This also I saw, that it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from the hand of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For who can eat, or who else can hasten ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " more than I?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.2.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.2.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " giveth to a man who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good in his sight, wisdom, and knowledge, and joy: but to the sinner he giveth toil, to gather, and to amass, that he may give to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good before God. This also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity and vexation of spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
